From 293e500819f0a861a5d4bed854f3a9884f928fd4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 11:30:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] WebPlayer: show the page in its own window and route input to
 it

The fullscreen video window's keymap turns every key into a playback
action and leaves nothing for the page. Add WINDOW_FULLSCREEN_WEB, a
window that draws the player like the video window does and knows that
the pointer belongs to the page, and make the application treat it like
the other fullscreen players when switching to fullscreen, cleaning up
after playback, reloading the skin and notifying the player of actions.
Its keymap section claims only the keys Kodi keeps: Escape and Menu
open the OSD, Home opens Kodi's home screen and leaves the page running.

While that window is active the player forwards every other key to the
client with its scan code, except a key bound globally to a Kodi
command or to the volume that types no character, and releases keys
still held when Kodi takes the input back. The colour keys always go to
the page, as TV pages drive their menus with them. Pointer positions go
to the client once per change, as an air mouse lying still keeps
reporting the same one, buttons are forwarded and the wheel becomes
axis events; Kodi keeps drawing its pointer, so motion is passed on to
the GUI as well. The view is active only while the web window is the
active window, so the client knows when nobody sees the page.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
